{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Final rebar-debug report (ticket intentionally left in_progress; closure deferred)\n\nProblem: an unchanged prerequisite pinned under a supported historical fingerprint generation was rejected as stale material drift.\n\nProven root cause: pin_health.derive_health compared the signed related pin only with the latest fingerprint generation. The attestation wrapper did not supply the existing _legacy_material_ok recomputation used for own-ticket attestations, so algorithm evolution alone took the stale-pin-drift branch.\n\nProof: runtime tracing of the real retired pin observed signed 6b113a084820af9d versus latest bbe91c054a677441, with no prerequisite event after review; recomputation of current material under the supported intermediate generation exactly matched the signed pin. Wrong-target, hidden-event, semantic-edit, and arbitrary-hash alternatives were rejected.\n\nTest: tests/unit/test_plan_material_pin_generation_3e0f.py was observed RED before repair only for the unchanged historical-generation case (1 failed/2 controls passed), held out from the fixer, then GREEN 3/3. Removing the compatibility predicate returned exactly that case to RED while semantic-edit and unmatched-hash controls stayed green; restoring it returned GREEN. Focused pin/attestation suite passed 64/64.\n\nFix: derive_health accepts an optional fail-closed compatibility predicate after latest-hash mismatch; the public attestation wrapper supplies _legacy_material_ok. A pin becomes current only if a supported historical recomputation of current material exactly matches it. Latest current_fingerprint reporting and the original pinned_fingerprint are preserved.\n\nScope/safety: all production callers route through the attestation wrapper; compute_validity, resign, claim/close/reuse/drift consumers are incidental and still reject genuine unmatched drift. The fix restores jira-reb-1160 intent, adds no dependency, weakens no test, and fails stale on compatibility exceptions. make lint/typecheck passed.\n\nSiblings/parity: own-ticket validity already used the same supported-generation rule; related-pin health was the only missing parallel surface. No other direct derive_health production wrapper or historical-generation comparison was found.\n\nReplication: the original real-store scenario now yields aggregate/target current; semantic edit and 0000000000000000 remain stale-pin-drift. The report no longer reproduces.\n\nLanding: Gerrit change 1564 received LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, had no unresolved comments, and was submitted/merged at 2026-08-09 18:51:48Z. No residual fragility observed beyond the fixed parity gap."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786301519188096001,"uuid":"273fd090-043f-426a-ba60-bf0853e3e411"}